CS 252 Lab 1 – Custom Memory Allocator
Student: Naman Kansal (kansal2)

FEATURES IMPLEMENTED

Base Features
• User-level replacement for malloc() and free()
• Manual heap memory management in user space
• Memory requested from the OS using low-level system calls
• Block-based heap organization with metadata headers

Memory Management
• Each heap block contains a metadata header
• Header stores block size and allocation status
• Integrity metadata used for validation and debugging
• Header-based layout enables heap traversal without external structures

Free List Organization
• Multiple free lists maintained for different size classes
• Free lists reduce allocation search time
• Small and large allocations handled independently

Allocation Strategy
• Requested sizes are aligned and normalized
• Appropriate free list selected based on size
• Suitable free block searched within the selected list
• Blocks split when larger than required
• Allocated portion returned to the user

Deallocation Strategy
• Freed blocks returned to appropriate free list
• Adjacent free blocks are coalesced
• Coalescing reduces external fragmentation
• Heap consistency maintained during free operations

Safety and Correctness
• Detection of invalid and double free operations
• Heap structure invariants preserved
• Metadata integrity checks included

CONCEPTS DEMONSTRATED
• Heap memory management
• Pointer arithmetic and alignment
• Free list–based allocators
• Internal and external fragmentation
• Block splitting and coalescing
• Low-level systems programming in C

BUILDING AND RUNNING

Build
make

Testing
./runtest.py

